{{wikipedia|dab=termination}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{L.}} ''[[terminationem]]'' (nominative of ''[[terminatio]]'').

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The process of [[terminating]] or the state of being [[terminate]]d.
# The process of firing an employee; ending one's employment at a business for any reason.
# An [[end]] in [[time]]; a [[conclusion]].
# An end in [[space]]; an [[edge]] or [[limit]].
# An [[outcome]] or [[result]].
# The last part of a [[word]]; a [[suffix]].
# {{medical}} An induced [[abortion]].

====Synonyms====
* (''process of terminating''): [[conclude|conluding]], [[end]]ing, [[finish]]ing, [[stop]]ing, [[terminate|terminating]]
* (''state of being termined''):
* (''end in time''): [[close]], [[conclusion]], [[end]], [[finale]], [[finish]], [[stop]]
* (''end in space''): [[border]], [[edge]], [[end]], [[limit]], [[lip]], [[rim]], [[tip]]
* (''outcome''): [[consequence]], [[outcome]], [[result]], [[upshot]]
* (''medical''): [[abortion]], [[induced abortion]]

